  "problem": "Given $X\u223c\\text{Geom}(0.15),$ compute $P(X=7).$  Round your final answer to $4$ decimal places.",
  "worked_solution": "If $X\u223c\\text{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,\u2026 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X\u223c\\text{Geom}(0.15),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}{(0.85)}^{x-1}(0.15), & x=1,2,3,\u2026 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=7) & =f(7) \\\\  & ={(0.85)}^{6}(0.15) \\\\  & \u22480.0566.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
